# Heroes

Four visual patterns. Do not invent a fifth without updating this file.

## 1. Home (cinematic, centered)

- `section` `min-h-[72vh]`, `aria-labelledby` pointing at the `h1`.
- Full-bleed `<img>`: `object-cover`, `fetchpriority="high"`, `decoding="async"`.
- `src` / `srcset` from `cardImageSrc` + `heroSrcset` (`/cdn-cgi/image/…`). `sizes="100vw"`.
- Intrinsic `width`/`height` must match the asset aspect (not a collapsed placeholder).
- Overlays: radial + linear dark gradients so cream type stays readable.
- Stack: kicker rules → `NOTOFILIA` wordmark (display) → diamond divider → `h1` (title, not the wordmark) → lead → optional **single** stats line → primary + secondary CTAs.
- Stats: at most one of (hero line, stats band). See `00-site-standards.mdc`.
- Alt from i18n, both locales.

## 2. Series (bottom-anchored full-bleed)

Used by country/series indexes (`*SeriesPage`, `*CoinagePage`, `LazarettosPage`). Polymer world is a documented **text-header** exception (discipline-like), not a third photo hero.

- `section` `min-h-[86vh] md:min-h-[94vh]`, `aria-labelledby` on the `h1`.
- Full-bleed photo with `object-cover` and an explicit `object-position`.
- Image **must** use `heroSrcset` / `cfImage` plus `sizes="100vw"`. Raw `/images/…` is a FAIL.
- `fetchpriority="high"`, real `width`/`height`, meaningful `alt` from series copy.
- Bottom-weighted radial + linear scrim. Type sits in the lower third (`justify-end`, `pt-[min(68vh,38rem)]`).
- Kicker: “Colección virtual” / “Virtual collection” from i18n (not a component literal).
- `h1`: stacked kicker + title spans, display face, text-shadow.
- Breadcrumbs go **below** the hero, inside the `article` case (`max-w-content`).

## 3. Piece (optional series hero, else text-first)

- If the piece has `hero`: reuse the series photo pattern (CDN URL, high fetch priority, alt).
- If not: no full-bleed section. Start with breadcrumbs + `h1` + lead (`max-w-[46rem]`).
- Catalog scans (anverso/reverso) use `NoteImageLightbox` at full resolution — not a hero.

## 4. About (color-block, no photo)

Used only by `AboutPage.astro` (`/acerca-de/`, `/en/about/`).

- Full-bleed `section` with `bg-alert` / `text-alert-ink` (`#d61f26` + white). No photograph and no fake LCP image.
- Inner case: `max-w-content` + `--page-gutter`. Lead stays about `40rem` / `640px`.
- Stack: uppercase kicker → stacked display `h1` (one line per `titleLines` span) → lead paragraph.
- `h1` size is clamped for mobile; the mock’s ~118px is desktop only.
- Breadcrumbs go **below** the red field, inside the `article` case (`max-w-content`). Do not place crumbs on the alert ground.
- Do not render `statsLine()` here. Live collection counts belong in the collector aside via `collectionStats()`.

## Types with no photo hero

`about` uses pattern 4 (color-block, live `--color-alert` / `--color-alert-ink`). `contact`, `collection-hub`, `discipline-index`, `editorial-index`, `glossary-*`, `search`, `stub`, `error` have no photo hero.

`editorial-article` uses an in-flow `<figure>` after the header, through `cardImageSrc` + `imageSrcset`. That is not a hero.

## Do not

- Ship a series/home LCP image without `/cdn-cgi/image/`.
- Duplicate the homepage stats line under the hero.
- Put breadcrumbs or a facts card on top of the photo.
- Recap the hero `h1` with a second page title immediately below unless the hero is decorative-only (it is not).
